id|cell_04
title|The Meeting and Strange Lights
v_from|17
v_to|30
scenes|scene_07_deal_with_kaito.txt;scene_08_afghanistan_battle.txt;scene_09_ufo_abduction.txt
beat|As night fell, Lucky met with informants in a marketplace near the western district; they spoke quietly of shipments, routes, and guarded compounds. One informant warned him, saying there were forces at work greater than the ambitions of warlords and the schemes of governments. Lucky answered that many men speak in riddles when they possess no facts; the informant replied that may God preserve him when the facts arrive. Afterwards Astra observed strange lights moving among the mountains, changing direction suddenly and moving without visible engines, unlike any aircraft known; she reported it to Lucky, and neither understood its meaning. In the following days rumors spread through the city of secret weapons, hidden armies, and visitors from the heavens; most dismissed such reports.

